 "source": "https://catalog.ucsb.edu/programs/BAPOLS",
 "narrative": [
  "To qualify for admission into full major status, students must complete three courses from Political Science 1, 6, 7, and 12, as well as Political Science 15 with a UC grade-point average of 2.6 or above. Economics 1 and 2 (or 9) must also be completed on a letter graded basis and are included in the overall major GPA, but are excluded from the pre-major grade-point average computation.",
  "MAJOR REGULATIONSPREREQUISITES Check the General Catalog for the prerequisites to all listed courses.\nP/NP GRADING OPTION Not allowed for any major courses, including courses applied to the major from other departments, with one exception: Up to 4 units of Pol S 192, Int 192DC, or 192SA (P/NP required) may be applied to the major (UD Area D).\nSUBSTITUTIONS In the major requirements permissible only by petition to the department chair and dean.\nG.P.A REQUIREMENTS At least 2.0 overall UC average in all upper-division major courses and all courses (Prep and UD) for the major.\nDOUBLE MAJORS With the approval of each department chairperson, up to a total of 8 units may be applied simultaneously to both UD majors"
 ],
